      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A reliable way to check is by placing your fingers lightly on your Adam's apple or your throat area while you produce the sounds. When you say /z/, you should feel a distinct, low-frequency vibration—a buzzing sensation—running through your throat. If you say /s/, you will feel only the rush of air, but no actual vibration from the tissue itself. It's like the difference between a noisy, wind-whistling passage and a low, vibrating hum.",
